  "title": "5 Wildly Different Trucks Reveal the Scope of Mopar’s Direct Connection Catalog",
  "summary": "It’s only appropriate that Brian Szalk, the man in charge of Ram’s factory-backed parts catalog, is restoring—and modifying—one of the earliest muscle trucks. His 1978 Dodge Li’l Red Express, which he bought in pieces, is getting a driveline transplant courtesy of a rear-ended 2017 Ram 1500, which is donating its 5.7-liter engine and eight-speed transmission. […]",
